{"paper": "SSC-SelectionPost-Phase12-Graduate-25-Jun-2024-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "∆PQR and ∆ABC are two congruent triangles. If the area of ∆PQR is 225 cm2 , then the area of ∆ABC is:", "options": [{"text": "15 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "225 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "112.5 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "25 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Simplify the expression: 15×15×15+3×15×12×12-3×15×15×12-12×12×12", "options": [{"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Suresh invested a certain sum of money at 5% per annum simple interest. If he receives an interest of ₹69687 after 15 year, the sum (in ₹) he invested is:", "options": [{"text": "92880", "added": false}, {"text": "92456", "added": false}, {"text": "92916", "added": false}, {"text": "92530", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "T he strength of a school increases and decreases every alternate year by 20%. It started with an increase in 2018. What is the strength of the school at the start of 2021 as compared to that of 2018?", "options": [{"text": "Increase by 16.2%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increase by 15.2%", "added": false}, {"text": "D ecrease by 16.2%", "added": false}, {"text": "D ecrease by 15.2%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "34", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "38", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A vendor buys 20 laptop bags for ₹13,000 and sells them at 15 for ₹10,125. How many laptop bags should be bought and sold to earn a profit of ₹3,225?", "options": [{"text": "120", "added": false}, {"text": "129", "added": false}, {"text": "123", "added": false}, {"text": "127", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A policeman notices a thief from a distance of 300 m. T he thief starts running and the policeman chases him. T he thief and the policeman run at the speeds of 10 km/h and 12 km/h, respectively. What will be the distance between them (in m) after 6 minutes?", "options": [{"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "200", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "relative-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "T he sides of a right-angled triangle, right-angled at B, are 6, 8 and 10 units. C is the vertex opposite to the side with length 8 units. What is the value of tan2 A + cos2 C?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "If μ = 60°, then Sinμ + Cos(90 - μ) = _______.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "complementary-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "T he average weight of Rohan and his three friends is 62 kg. If Rohan’s weight is 8 kg more than the average weight of his three friends, what is Rohan’s weight (in kg)?", "options": [{"text": "68", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "72", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "T he fourth proportional of 64, 80 and 88 is:", "options": [{"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "120", "added": false}, {"text": "110", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "An old HP Deskjet printer was bought for ₹4,800 and ₹500 was spent on its repair. If it was sold for ₹6,360, then its profit percentage is:", "options": [{"text": "0.12", "added": false}, {"text": "0.15", "added": false}, {"text": "0.18", "added": false}, {"text": "0.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1450", "added": false}, {"text": "1625", "added": false}, {"text": "1520", "added": false}, {"text": "1850", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "If three angles of a triangle are (18x+6°), (10x+30°) and (15x+15°), then the triangle is:", "options": [{"text": "right angled", "added": false}, {"text": "scalene", "added": false}, {"text": "isosceles", "added": false}, {"text": "equilateral", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "56.0", "added": false}, {"text": "56.33", "added": false}, {"text": "55.5", "added": false}, {"text": "54.33", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "Nazeer spends 20% of his monthly income on housing, 25% of the remaining on education, and saves 10% of the remaining. If his monthly salary is ₹52,600, how much money does he save every month?", "options": [{"text": "₹3,156", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,367", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,260", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,578", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "T he number 7918378 is divisible by:", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "A and B can do a piece of work in 10 days. B and C can do the same work in 12 days. C and A can do the same work in 15 days. If all the three work together, find the number of days required to complete the work.", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "What least number must be subtracted from 2001 to get a number exactly divisible by 17?", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "Who among the following scored the maximum overall percentage?", "options": [{"text": "Sanjana", "added": false}, {"text": "Simran", "added": false}, {"text": "Jyoti", "added": false}, {"text": "Bhumika", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "T he average monthly income of A and B is ₹5,050, the average monthly income of B and C is ₹6,250, and the average monthly income of A and C is ₹5,200. What is the sum of the monthly incomes (in ₹) of A, B and C?", "options": [{"text": "16500", "added": false}, {"text": "18000", "added": false}, {"text": "11000", "added": false}, {"text": "19500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "A tractor manufacturing company sells each tractor for ₹5,00,000. Assuming that KISAN firm buys 50 tractors from them as a part of an annual contract, the company offers a trade discount of 10% to KISAN and an additional 2% discount if the payment is made within 30 days. What will be the amount payable by KISAN within 30 days for the consignment?", "options": [{"text": "₹22,080,100", "added": false}, {"text": "₹22,050,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹20,051,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹24,050,020", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "21 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "18 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "27 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "24 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}]}